Getting Started
Prerequisites
PHP 7.4 or newer
MySQL or MariaDB
A local server stack such as XAMPP, WAMP or Laragon (or Apache/Nginx with PHP)
Composer
Installation
Clone the repository
bash
   git clone https://github.com/mizaraihanah/rotiserifypinventory.git
   cd rotiserifypinventory
Place the project in your web server folder For example, htdocs/ for XAMPP.
Install dependencies
bash
   composer install
Create the database
Create a new database (e.g. roti_seri_bakery_inventory).
Import the SQL file included in the repository, either through phpMyAdmin (Import tab) or the command line:
bash
     mysql -u root -p roti_seri_bakery_inventory < "roti_seri_bakery_inventory (9).sql"
Configure the application Open db_connection.php and config.php and set your own values:
Database host, name, username and password
SMTP settings (host, port, username, password) for password-reset emails

